––– comment –––
Every node started once (one 'forked ok' of the watchdog), its process was never killed by a signal ('killed dirtily', also an abort of the replication provider, which leaves no crash dump) and it wrote no crash dump: no node crashed and came back by a restart
––– input –––
for n in 1 2 3; do L=/var/log/manticore-$n/searchd.log; echo "node $n starts=$(grep -c 'watchdog: main process .* forked ok' $L) killed=$(grep -c 'killed dirtily' $L) dumps=$(grep -c 'CRASH DUMP' $L)"; done
––– output –––
node 1 starts=1 killed=0 dumps=0
node 2 starts=1 killed=0 dumps=0
node 3 starts=1 killed=0 dumps=0
